  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P><IMG src="http://us.news2.yimg.com/us.yimg.com/p/ap/20040915/capt.jrl10109151331.mideast_israel_palestinians_madonna_jrl101.jpg" align=left border=0>We previously published her letter to <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>. </P>
<P>Now we show you a pic - on the left -&nbsp;showing <STRONG>Angela</STRONG> protesting against the scheduled visit of <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> to <STRONG>Rachel</STRONG>’s tomb which is located in the <STRONG>West Bank</STRONG> town of <STRONG>Bethlehem</STRONG>, as they stand at the checkpoint between <STRONG>Jerusalem</STRONG> and the biblical town, Wednesday, Sept. 15, 2004. </P>
<P>The protesters wanted to point out that the site is in the <STRONG>West Bank</STRONG> and draw attention to the plight of Palestinians living under Israeli military control.</P>
<P>The pic below shows an unidentified woman holds a placard protesting.</P>
<P><IMG src="http://us.news2.yimg.com/us.yimg.com/p/ap/20040915/capt.jrl10209151331.mideast_israel_palestinians_madonna_jrl102.jpg" align=right border=0></P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P><IMG src="http://us.news2.yimg.com/us.yimg.com/p/ap/20040915/capt.jrl10409151347.mideast_israel_palestinians_madonna_jrl104.jpg" align=right border=0>On the right you can see Israeli soldiers providing security as members of the <STRONG>Ecumenical Accompaniment Program in Palestine and Israel</STRONG>, a non-governmental organization, demonstrate against the scheduled visit of <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> to Rachel’s tomb, seen in background. The banner reads in Hebrew and Arabic: <STRONG>’Peace.’</STRONG> </P>
</font></div>
