 <table width="100%" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" cellpadding="5">
  <tr>
    <td background="images/bg.gif"><font class=""><a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=6">Magazines</a></font><br><font class="testo_notizia" color="#000000"><b>Church's Madonna ambition.</b></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td  background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><SPAN class=byline><IMG src="http://www.megastar.co.uk/ents/news/2004/08/05/sMEG01MTA5MTcwMzUwNTU.jpg" align=left border=0>Wyndham King/ <STRONG>MegaStar</STRONG></SPAN><BR><BR><!-- body text goes here --><SPAN class=body>
<P class=body>
<TABLE cellSpacing=0 cellPadding=5 width=120 align=right border=0>
<TBODY>
<TR>
<TD class=white><STRONG></STRONG></TD></TR>
<TR>
<TD><STRONG></STRONG></TD></TR>
<TR>
<TD class=essential><STRONG></STRONG></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE><STRONG>Welsh warbler Charlotte Church's mother says she hopes her daughter will be even bigger than Madonna. </STRONG></P>
<P class=body></P>
<P class=body>A few more burgers should do it, then.</P>
<P class=body></P>
<P class=body>That's some ambition, though, love. And you'd better brush up on your Kabbalah to get on the right track.</P>
<P class=body></P>
<P class=body>Tipple-tasting loony-lungster Charlotte has, of course, given up the angelic trilling that made granny put down her knitting, in favour of a fledgling pop career - and all the raunchy nonsense that goes with it.</P>
<P class=body></P>
<P class=body>This involves turning herself into a bad girl, as the Sun puts it, and is clearly where the boys, booze and fags come in.</P>
<P class=body></P>
<P class=body><STRONG>Her doting mum Maria confirms in the paper that her girl plans to be more successful than her idol, the Madgester</STRONG>. And there's a tale of the tape thingy to see how the, er, rivals, tally up.</P>
<P class=body></P>
<P class=body><STRONG>Suffice to say, Madonna's considerably richer than Churchy, isn't from Wales, is 28 years older than young missy and has the same sized sauce-shelf.</STRONG></P>
<P class=body></P>
<P class=body>Inconclusive, eh?</P></SPAN>
</font></div>
	</td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td background="images/bg.gif" align="center"><font class="content">Written by <a href="">gugarko</a> on 2004-09-14 13:19:31 W. Europe Standard Time  [37 reads].</font><br>
<font class="content">(<a href="modules.php?name=News&amp;file=article&amp;sid=4400"><b>Read More...</b></a> | <a href="modules.php?name=News&amp;file=article&amp;sid=4400">4 comments</a> | Score: 0)</font></td>
  </tr>
</table>
<br><br><br>


 <table width="100%" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" cellpadding="5">
  <tr>
    <td background="images/bg.gif"><font class=""><a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=22">Books</a></font><br><font class="testo_notizia" color="#000000"><b>[<a href="modules.php?name=&amp;file=categories&amp;op=newindex&amp;catid=1"><font class="esclusiva">ESCLUSIVA</font></a>] Yakov e i Sette Ladroni.</b></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td  background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P align=center><IMG src="http://www.drownedmadonna.com/images/mele/YakovEISetteLadri.jpg" border=0></P>
<P>We can reveal that the final cover of the <STRONG>Italian edition</STRONG> of <STRONG>"Yakov and the Seven Thieves"</STRONG> is different from the <STRONG>work-in-progress</STRONG>&nbsp;one (see the scan above)&nbsp;that&nbsp; <STRONG>Drowned Madonna</STRONG> exclusively published on <FONT size=2><STRONG>2003/11/24 - <A href="http://www.drownedmadonna.com/modules.php?name=News&amp;file=article&amp;sid=932">LINK</A></STRONG>&nbsp;- it features a different illustration.&nbsp;This work-in-progress cover was also&nbsp;published on the back of the Italian edition of <STRONG>"Mr Peabody's Apples"</STRONG>. </FONT></P>
<P><FONT size=2><STRONG>Even the title of the book has changed from "Yakov e i Sette LADRI" to "Yakov e i Sette LADRONI".</STRONG></FONT></P>
<P><FONT size=2>However, that illustration has been used for the page where the kid&nbsp;can write his/her name.</FONT></P>
<P><FONT size=2>We can also reveal the book&nbsp;presention by <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> and the book opening as it is published on the Italian edition of this children book. <STRONG>Italian translations courtesy of the editor.</STRONG></FONT></P>
<P><FONT size=2><STRONG>PRESENTATION:</STRONG></FONT></P>
<P><FONT size=2>Questo libro si ispira al Baal Shem Tov, un grande maestro che visse in Ucraina nel XVIII secolo.</FONT></P>
<P><FONT size=2>Racconta che chiunque di noi è in grado di aprire i cancelli del Paradiso, per quanto non se ne ritenga degno. Perché chi riesce a superare il proprio egoismo può fare miracoli, nella propria vita e in quella degli altri.</FONT></P>
<P><FONT size=2>Non dobbiamo mai dimenticare che dietro una grande oscurità c'è sempre una grande luce.</FONT></P>
<P align=right><FONT size=2>Madonna</FONT></P>
<P><FONT size=2><STRONG>OPENING:</STRONG></FONT></P>
<P><FONT size=2>C'ERA UNA VOLTA, IN UN minuscolo villaggio nascosto tra due montagne, un ciabattino di nome Yakov. Dalla sua bottega poteva ammirare la bellezza del paesaggio che lo circondava: le foreste magiche, i ruscelli cristallini e le maestose cime innevate che si ergevano in lontananza.</FONT></P>
<P><FONT size=2>Yakov aveva un figlio, Mikhail, un bambino così malato che era costretto a rimanere sempre a letto, e così debole che non riusciva a muoversi né parlare. Nell'ultimo anno Yakov e sua moglie Olga non avevano fatto altro che consultare medici in cerca di una cura. Ma la malattia del figlio restava un mistero. <STRONG>Yakov si rese conto che era giunto il momento di prendere in mano la situazione.</STRONG></FONT></P>
<P align=center><STRONG>ITALIAN RELEASE DATE: 16TH SEPTEMBER 2004</STRONG></P>
<P align=left><STRONG><EM>A Drowned Madonna exclusive. </EM></STRONG></P>
</font></div>
	</td>
  </tr>
